        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> That sounds great. It would certainly help, but I would still like an option to display no warning at all. But that's completely personal, and I would fully respect if you decided to not add that option.\r\n> \r\n> Thanks for the fast reply :)\r\n\r\nI also considered adding a unified `verbose` options to all modules producing such help messages. If `false`, it would not show them.\r\n\r\nI will start with updating message logic to not result into hit-enter-prompt and think about not showing messages later.\r\n\r\nTo add. The reasoning behind showing this warning is for user to be aware that textobject is not found within `n_lines` lines and using current search method. Because it can cause confusion when textobject is large and don't fit inside searched neighborhood. Same goes for 'mini.surround'. ",
